The NVENC backend (src/nvenc.rs and src/nvenc_ffi/), the Annex B helpers (src/annexb.rs), the
HEVC parameter-set reading (src/hevc.rs) and the layout tests (src/nvenc_ffi/abi_tests.rs) come
from FilmCraft's `crates/platform/src/nvenc/` (https://github.com/storytold/filmcraft, commit
de529c88f4948d0803bef746a325707f2671a71d), MIT OR Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team
and the FilmCraft contributors.

The Media Foundation loading, COM setup, sample creation, MFT enumeration and output reading in
src/mf_ffi/api.rs and src/mf_ffi/transform.rs come from FilmCraft's
`crates/platform/src/media_foundation/mft.rs` and `gpu.rs` (same repository, commit and license).

The VideoToolbox session setup, pixel buffer filling, output callback and parameter-set reading in
src/vt_ffi/session.rs come from FilmCraft's `crates/platform/src/videotoolbox_encode.rs` (same
repository, commit and license).

The libva loading, DRM display opening and render node listing in src/vaapi_ffi/session.rs come
from FilmCraft's `crates/platform/src/vaapi/va.rs` and `ffi.rs` (same repository, commit and
license).

The libva base declarations in src/vaapi_ffi/abi.rs come from FilmCraft's
`crates/platform/src/vaapi/ffi.rs` (same repository, commit and license). The encode structures
added to them are transcribed from libva's headers.

The declarations in src/nvenc_ffi/abi.rs are transcribed from NVIDIA's `nvEncodeAPI.h` (Video
Codec SDK, API 12.1), Copyright (c) 2010-2023 NVIDIA Corporation, under the MIT license whose
text is at the top of that file.

The declarations in src/vaapi_ffi/abi.rs are transcribed from libva's `va.h`, `va_enc_h264.h`,
`va_enc_hevc.h` and `va_drm.h` (libva 2.22.0), Copyright (c) 2007-2009 Intel Corporation, and
`va_enc_av1.h` (libva 2.22.0), Copyright (c) 2021 Intel Corporation, under the MIT license whose
text is at the top of that file.
